  message: "Resolved the db_*-taxonomy + FP scope in PR #685 (dev a58b18f82a; CI green, 2950 tests / 100% coverage). Owner-ratified clean-scope (2026-07-16).\n\n(A) Python stdlib db_read/db_write populated (sqlite3/dbm/shelve) — the db_* category is no longer empty for Python (it was always in CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES and populated for 6 other language catalogs; Python was the gap). (B) django.core.management.execute_from_command_line net_recv FP removed.\n\nPRODUCTION-PATH behavioral evidence (`hypergumbo io-boundaries` on a sqlite3+dbm fixture): boundary keys=[db_read], db_read chains=[dbm.open, sqlite3.connect], total_io_edges=2 (was []/0 pre-PR); execute_from_command_line present=False. Unit guards: test_tags_sqlite3_connect_as_db_read / test_tags_dbm_open_as_db_read / test_python_catalog_drops_execute_from_command_line_fp (green).\n\nTRANSFERRED, NOT CLOSED: the dominant symptom in THIS item body (Django ORM / cache / most net I/O invisible -> io_tag_rate ~0.5% on pretix) is a DISTINCT receiver-inference problem this PR does NOT resolve, refiled as WI-sozoj-vabud-dovaf-nagot-tonod-gobov-godap-pamot (P2, wave5). Verified against pretix live survey: 90%+ of ORM calls are bare untyped unresolved external method calls the io-boundary matcher CORRECTLY refuses (INV-tapat); catalog entries cannot reach them. Honest facet-close (db_* taxonomy + FP behaviorally verified); the metric/ORM facet has a named owner, not a proxy close."  # f4c1
